id=a52sxq_kernel_bone_machine
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: bone-machine kernel 5.4.302
author=CodesRahul96
description=Replaces the stock A528BXXU5FWK4 kernel (Linux 5.4.233, Nov 2023) with bone-machine's One UI kernel, Linux 5.4.302-bone-machine-qgki (final 5.4 LTS sublevel), built from source (https://github.com/mna08072-cmyk/android_kernel_samsung_sm7325_a52s_5g branch resukisu-oneui @93b49d0ccd89, ReSukiSU 35203; upstream bone-machine/android_kernel_samsung_sm7325_a52s_5g) plus k4 patches (CAP_PERFMON/CAP_BPF/CAP_CHECKPOINT_RESTORE, GPU NAP and stock GPU voltage/315 MHz init level restored, KGSL idle timeout 80 ms, BTF for Android 17's BPF CPU-time tracking: CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_BTF with 5.4-compatible pahole kinds, BPF_MAP_TYPE_RINGBUF backport for Google's Tethering APEX, KernelSU stat hook on native newfstatat/statx so su works; since 2026-10-18 also 0008 battery pass_through node for One UI's "pause USB PD charging" and 0009-0016 the USB gadget UVC webcam function used by patches/usb_webcam). Artifact prebuilts/kernel/bone-machine/bone-machine_k4btf_ringbuf_su_pt_uvc8_test_a52sxq.zip ("_test" is only the build series name), sha256 af1e005a6855b634670d93f9564271c795524233da5ad55e6d401eacfd4a99a4, k4 patches 0001-0016 (recipe and .config: see SOURCE.txt). Swaps only the kernel Image inside our boot.img (our ramdisk, cmdline and 2023-11 OS patch level stay), and uses the release's vendor_boot.img (same first-stage fstab, its 84 modules rebuilt for this kernel incl. wlan.ko, matching dtb) and dtbo.img. NOTE: the kernel has ReSukiSU (KernelSU fork) built in (dormant without its manager app) and Samsung Knox/RKP/KDP/DEFEX/PROCA/FIVE/DSMS disabled.
